From: Jian Zhang <zhangjian.3032@bytedance.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Mar 2026 14:06:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ncsi: fix skb leak in error paths
Git-commit: 5c3398a54266541610c8d0a7082e654e9ff3e259
Patch-mainline: v7.0-rc4
References: CVE-2026-43373 bsc#1265079

Early return paths in NCSI RX and AEN handlers fail to release
the received skb, resulting in a memory leak.

Specifically, ncsi_aen_handler() returns on invalid AEN packets
without consuming the skb. Similarly, ncsi_rcv_rsp() exits early
when failing to resolve the NCSI device, response handler, or
request, leaving the skb unfreed.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Fixes: 7a82ecf4cfb8 ("net/ncsi: NCSI AEN packet handler")
Fixes: 138635cc27c9 ("net/ncsi: NCSI response packet handler")
Signed-off-by: Jian Zhang <zhangjian.3032@bytedance.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260305060656.3357250-1-zhangjian.3032@bytedance.com
Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
---
 net/ncsi/ncsi-aen.c |    3 ++-
 net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c |   16 ++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/net/ncsi/ncsi-aen.c
+++ b/net/ncsi/ncsi-aen.c
@@ -208,7 +208,8 @@ int ncsi_aen_handler(struct ncsi_dev_pri
 	if (!nah) {
 		netdev_warn(ndp->ndev.dev, "Invalid AEN (0x%x) received\n",
 			    h->type);
-		return -ENOENT;
+		ret = -ENOENT;
+		goto out;
 	}
 
 	ret = ncsi_validate_aen_pkt(h, nah->payload);
--- a/net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c
+++ b/net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c
@@ -974,8 +974,10 @@ int ncsi_rcv_rsp(struct sk_buff *skb, st
 	/* Find the NCSI device */
 	nd = ncsi_find_dev(dev);
 	ndp = nd ? TO_NCSI_DEV_PRIV(nd) : NULL;
-	if (!ndp)
-		return -ENODEV;
+	if (!ndp) {
+		ret = -ENODEV;
+		goto err_free_skb;
+	}
 
 	/* Check if it is AEN packet */
 	hdr = (struct ncsi_pkt_hdr *)skb_network_header(skb);
@@ -997,7 +999,8 @@ int ncsi_rcv_rsp(struct sk_buff *skb, st
 	if (!nrh) {
 		netdev_err(nd->dev, "Received unrecognized packet (0x%x)\n",
 			   hdr->type);
-		return -ENOENT;
+		ret = -ENOENT;
+		goto err_free_skb;
 	}
 
 	/* Associate with the request */
@@ -1005,7 +1008,8 @@ int ncsi_rcv_rsp(struct sk_buff *skb, st
 	nr = &ndp->requests[hdr->id];
 	if (!nr->used) {
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ndp->lock, flags);
-		return -ENODEV;
+		ret = -ENODEV;
+		goto err_free_skb;
 	}
 
 	nr->rsp = skb;
@@ -1029,4 +1033,8 @@ int ncsi_rcv_rsp(struct sk_buff *skb, st
 out:
 	ncsi_free_request(nr);
 	return ret;
+
+err_free_skb:
+	kfree_skb(skb);
+	return ret;
 }
